pr_comments:
> > It still fetches signature from default. Stepping through in debugger, in do_sigver_init, iteration 1, it gets the default signature and tries to export which fails. On iteration 2, evp_signature_fetch_from_porv() still picks it from default and gives up. The provider passed to it is correct (my provider), keymgmt on the ctx is also now my provider. Line 137 of do_sigver_init.
> 
> Is the libctx used to load the key the same one as used for libssl?

Yes, same libctx for loading the provider, ssl_ctx and loading the key. The provider also loads default into the same libctx. The application may be implicitly using default provider in libctx=NULL too, but not related to this key. 

One thing though, the key is loaded via keymgmt_import and some custom parameters that keymgmt_import can parse (not store->keymgmt_load) -- slightly edited code below:

```
    const char *propq = "provider=ovpn.xkey";
    const char *type_name = EVP_PKEY_get0_type_name(pubkey);

    EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx = EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name(xkey_libctx, type_name, propq); /* this fetches the right keymgmt */
    EVP_PKEY_fromdata_init(ctx);
    EVP_PKEY_fromdata(ctx, &pkey, EVP_PKEY_KEYPAIR, params);
```

Under debugger the key delivered to do_sigver_init() looks all good.

